  "notes": "USAGE:\nA direct, somewhat informal word for falling in love or being captivated. More spontaneous and passionate than {好|す}きになる. Often implies being struck by sudden attraction.\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- {一目惚|ひとめぼ}れ: love at first sight\n- {惚|ほ}れ{込|こ}む: to fall deeply in love / to be thoroughly captivated\n- {惚|ほ}れ{惚|ぼ}れする: to be enchanted, to gaze in admiration\n- {惚|ほ}れた{弱|よわ}み: the weakness of being in love\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\nIchidan verb. Intransitive. Takes に for the object of affection: Xに{惚|ほ}れる.",
